// M5-A3P-1003. Ch18 K03 "Reedhollow: through the gate" (C, 2 min) and K04 "The new shell" (C,
// 3 min). act3_ch18.md §2 K03-K04; pell.md. The same gate as Ch10 (ch10_pell_kept_out): Pell walks in FIRST this
// time. The clutch doesn't stop him; they turn to see who it is. Owa meets him at the clutch's stone. The name-carver
// (Ch10's, the one who scraped his shell blank) carves the new one. The scraped shell goes into the lagoon and PELL DOES
// NOT WATCH IT SINK: he turns his back, the first time. Costume state change: the new shell (pell.md).
// RULE 5: held light; nothing rises here (the farewell-tide is K05, and taught, not performed).
title: ch18_through_the_gate
location: ch10/reedhollow
---
@letterbox on
@camera K05
@music reedhollow_return fade=2.0
@mark pell pell_gate walk
@wait 3.0
@mark pell clutch walk
@anim kirru turn_to pell
@wait 4.0
@camera K06
@mark owa clutch_stone walk
@wait 2.0
<<if $ch10_pell_kept_out>>
    Owa as "The eldest" [neutral]: You came in by yourself. Last time you waited to be told. #line:ch18_gate_001
<<endif>>
Pell [neutral]: Next time, I will turn around. #line:ch18_gate_002
@wait 3.0
Owa as "The eldest" [neutral]: Then you may have your name back. #line:ch18_gate_003
<<if $ch11_pell_knelt>>
    Owa as "The eldest" [sad]: We heard where you knelt. Under the old city. Before her. #line:ch18_gate_004
    @wait 2.0
<<endif>>
@camera K07
@mark kirru clutch_stone_b walk
Kirru as "Name-carver" [neutral]: I scraped this one. My hands remember. Let them carve it. #line:ch18_gate_005
@anim kirru carve name_shell
@wait 5.0
@camera K08
@anim pell take name_shell
@wait 2.0
@anim pell throw old_shell
@anim pell turn_back lagoon
@sfx shell_into_water
@wait 5.0
Pell [neutral]: Pell. #line:ch18_gate_006 #tn:"He says his own name once, as it is given back. Plain, not triumphant."
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch18_pell_named = true>>
@letterbox off
===
